{
  "version": 1,
  "discord_build": null,
  "_comment": [
    "Maps Discord's obfuscated CSS class names to the stable names the native client emits.",
    "Maintained themes target hashed names; ClearVision v7 keeps 3,198 of them in a single",
    "generated Sass map for exactly this reason. This file is the same idea in JSON.",
    "",
    "Maintenance: once per Discord client build, scrape the emitted :root and class list, then",
    "add an entry per name. `dcrs-port theme --class-map` reports the unmapped remainder, which",
    "is the work queue.",
    "",
    "The legacy BetterDiscord `[class*=\"prefix\"]` corpus does not need entries here: those",
    "selectors match on the human-readable prefix, so emitting `channel-`, `guilds-`,",
    "`messageContent-` etc. natively makes them work unchanged."
  ],
  "entries": {
    "guilds-a1": { "stable": "guilds", "surface": "guild-bar" },
    "guildsList-2f": { "stable": "guildsList", "surface": "guild-bar" },
    "panels-31": { "stable": "panels", "surface": "guild-bar" },
    "sidebar_a1": { "stable": "sidebar", "surface": "channel-list" },
